                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "5eb1b347-c01f-488d-a805-f45614e04d01",
                                "sense_id": "2a47523d-842d-30e1-a22e-cfbf4453b789",
                                "text": "So geriethen wir in die Jagdgeſchichten, von denen eine immer die andere nach ſich zog; nur einmal, in einer Pauſe des Geſpräches, ſagte Frau Chriſtine wie aus langem Sinnen: „Ob wohl noch die Kathe da iſt, am Ende der Straße, und das Aſtloch in der Hausthüre, durch das ich abends hinausſah, ob nicht mein Vater von der Arbeit komme? – Ich möcht’ doch einmal wieder hin!“",
                                "translation": "Thus we came up with hunting stories, one of which always followed the other; only once, after a pause in the conversation, Ms. Christine said as after a long muse: “I’m wondering whether the small cottage at the end of the street still exists, and the knothole in the front door through which I looked out evenings to see if my father was coming home from work? – I want to go there again!”",
                                "english": "Thus we came up with hunting stories, one of which always followed the other; only once, after a pause in the conversation, Ms. Christine said as after a long muse: “I’m wondering whether the small cottage at the end of the street still exists, and the knothole in the front door through which I looked out evenings to see if my father was coming home from work? – I want to go there again!”"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
